    "Corrected s009's target head from 'fiery' to 'serpent'. Rule 31's tie-break makes the ASV's bare 'serpent' for נָחָשׁ in this passage evidence that 'serpent' is the class noun realizing the lexeme, on the JOB.4.10-11 precedent; the accepted unit cited that same fact as a reason to head on the modifier, which inverts the rule. The competing reading (head on 'fiery', supported by שָׂרָף → bare 'fiery' at 21.6) is named in the unit's note under rule 8.",
